<article class="env-lemma" id="0BNK">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BNK">Lemma <span data-tag="0BNK">15.90.9</span>.</a> Let $R \to R'$ be a ring map. Let $I \subset R$ be an ideal such that $R/I^ n \to R'/I^ nR'$ is an isomorphism for $n > 0$. For any $I$-power torsion $R$-module $M$ the map $M \to M \otimes _ R R'$ is an isomorphism. For example, if $I$ is finitely generated and $R^\wedge $ is the completion of $R$ with respect to $I$, then we have $M \cong M \otimes _ R R^\wedge $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $M$ is annihilated by $I^ n$, then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  M \otimes _ R R' \cong M \otimes _{R/I^ n} R'/I^ n R' \cong M \otimes _{R/I^ n} R/I^ n \cong M.  \]
</div>
    <p>
       If $M$ is $I$-power torsion, then $M = \bigcup M[I^ n]$. Since tensor products commute with direct limits (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00DD" data-tag="00DD">10.12.9</a>), we obtain the desired isomorphism. The last statement is a special case of the first statement by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/05GG" data-tag="05GG">10.96.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>